<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682/1.0.0> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "TODO: citation of the accompanying publication" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "TODO: co-authors" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-08-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "TODO: author name, ORCID" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Ontology design pattern for the formalised description of technical processes according to VDI/VDE 3682 Part 1 (concept and graphic representation) and Part 2 (information model), issue May 2015.\n\nThe pattern covers the process network of states and process operators, the technical resources realising the operators, the system limit bounding the observation horizon, and the attribute structure of identification and characteristics.\n\nThe pattern is one of four subdomain patterns of the AIAS information model, which describes AI applications in automated plants together with the automated plant and the technical process. It is designed to be imported through owl:imports and aligned by way of the AIAS alignment ontology."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "TODO: institution" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> "TODO: funding statement, projects EKI and OptiFlex, dtec.bw" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www.vdi.de/richtlinien/details/vdivde-3682-blatt-1-formalisierte-prozessbeschreibungen-konzept-und-grafische-darstellung> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "VDI 3682 Ontology Design Pattern"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/status> "Draft"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "vdi3682" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: VDI/VDE 3682 Part 1 and Part 2, issue May 2015.\n\nRelation to prior work: this pattern is built independently but adopts several design decisions from the VDI 3682 ODP of the Institute of Automation Technology at Helmut Schmidt University (https://github.com/hsu-aut/IndustrialStandard-ODP-VDI3682, MIT licence). Adopted are the property chains for predecessor, successor, sub process and upper process, the defined class axiom for ProcessOperator, the dependency property expressing conjunction between states under the open world assumption, and the attribute structure of Identification and Characteristic.\n\nStructural deviations from that pattern are deliberate and documented at the affected elements: flows are reified as classes rather than expressed as object properties, assignments are reified as classes, and the system limit carries an explicit containment relation. See the notes on Flow, Assignment and SystemLimit."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0.0" .
