# https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ParallelFlow> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A flow that is part of a separate flow denoting mutually exclusive process paths."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alternative Flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.2.2 models alternative process runs as separate flows, again without additional graphical elements. Introducing a class for the alternative flow is a design decision of this pattern. Where alternative flows are present, the system limit must not be used as a balance limit."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment
