<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An operation transforming the input state of products, energies or information into an output state. The process operator realises this transformation by means of technical resources."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Process Operator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1. Only process operators may be decomposed; states are not decomposed (Part 1, Section 2).\n\nThe defined class axiom follows the VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University: anything with an input and an output that is contained in a process is a process operator. Anything with an input and an output alone may also be a process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Things of the real world that are transformed within a technical process. The generic term also covers flows of materials and substances."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemLimit> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The condition of a product, an energy or an information at a given point of a process, either as the status ante operationem before a transformation or as the status post operationem after it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "State"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 2, Figure 2 carries state as a class of the information model. Part 1, Section 4.1 deliberately avoids the term in the graphical notation because it is considered ambiguous there, and works with product, energy and information directly. This pattern follows Part 2."@en .
